    "subtitle": "Sharing responsibilities · 3",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to agree who will help whom after a change of circumstances.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U4-03-skill-K-HSK4-pragmatics-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "HSK 4: pragmatics",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Choose a degree of directness for the actual relationship and setting. A public contact and a close personal request need not use the same opening or assumption of obligation.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "对方",
                "pinyin": "duìfāng",
                "meaning": "the other person; the other side",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "b163da566956ee67333b1c9a9cc1c1d7507cf7fb1b15619bd61975254353af6e"
              },
              {
                "text": "感谢",
                "pinyin": "gǎnxiè",
                "meaning": "to thank; to be grateful",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "5ab62d6a6970cddd540f0e3ef6b4b9d6cc4700ae3ffd55a86a426956c96b6374"
              },
              {
                "text": "联系",
                "pinyin": "liánxì",
                "meaning": "connection; contact",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "651bfb762210180e712362ca6164410d84525c667ee904a8fbd1d7e5c7636ade"
              },
              {
                "text": "您",
                "pinyin": "nín",
                "meaning": "you, used respectfully",
                "singleWord": true,
                "audio": "f16b233bd9075387fbef9b385417347443ced956f316fe0b7a7253d5e84e8a20"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "You need to contact someone again tomorrow. First ask a close friend; then ask a person assisting visitors whom you do not know personally. Keep the same practical request and explain how your address or directness changes. Neither person has already agreed.\nFamiliar meanings available: the other person; the other side; to thank; to be grateful; connection; contact; you, used respectfully."
          }
        ]
      },
